    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior:** When a request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, the controller skips the 409 conflict that normally rejects a new owner whose `lastName` + `address` match an existing owner. Every created owner is assigned a `householdId` \u2014 a stable, deterministic identifier derived from the SHA-256 of the normalized `lastName` + `address`, so any owners in the same household get the identical value. The `householdId` is persisted and returned in the owner representation.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `householdId` field (mapped to a `household_id` column) with getter/setter, mirroring the existing `customerCode` pattern.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 hoisted the normalized last-name/address keys, set `householdId(...)` on every create, and added a `householdId(...)` helper producing `HH-<12 upper-hex>` from `SHA-256(lastNameKey|addressKey)`. Reused the existing `normalizeIdentity` normalization so households match consistently.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema (this drives the generated `OwnerDto`, which MapStruct maps automatically by name).\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The acceptance test confirms two `sharesHousehold` joiners at the same address/last name receive the same non-blank `householdId`.",
